.TH tkuaction n 0.2 tkutils
.SH tkutils::tkuaction
.PP
Action abstraction: define a UI action once \-\- label, command, icon, accelerator, enabled/checked state \-\- and register any number of widgets against it. A single \fBsetEnabled\fR / \fBsetChecked\fR / \fBinvoke\fR then keeps every registered widget in sync. This module is the \fBmodel\fR; rendering stays in the widgets, so there is no duplicated toolbar/menu code. Pure Tk.
.SS "Define / query"
.CS
::tkutils::tkuaction::define save -label "Save" -command {saveDoc} \
    ?-accelerator "Ctrl+S"? ?-icon img? ?-iconChecked img? ?-tooltip s? \
    ?-checkable 0|1? ?-enabled 0|1? ?-checked 0|1? ?-compound side?
::tkutils::tkuaction::exists save                 ;# 0|1
::tkutils::tkuaction::get    save ?key?           ;# whole dict or one field
::tkutils::tkuaction::names                        ;# all action names
::tkutils::tkuaction::delete save
.CE
.PP
A tooltip is derived from the label (plus accelerator) when not given.
.SS "State (the heart)"
.CS
::tkutils::tkuaction::setEnabled save 0|1 ?$w?     ;# greys every bound widget; with $w only that toplevel
::tkutils::tkuaction::setChecked wrap 0|1          ;# pressed look / iconChecked swap
::tkutils::tkuaction::getEnabled save ?$w?
::tkutils::tkuaction::getChecked wrap
::tkutils::tkuaction::toggle     wrap
::tkutils::tkuaction::invoke     save              ;# runs command if enabled; toggles if checkable
.CE
.SS "Bind widgets"
.CS
::tkutils::tkuaction::register   save $widget       ;# usually done by the widget
::tkutils::tkuaction::unregister save $widget
.CE
.PP
\fBtkutils::tkutoolbar::addAction $tb save\fR creates a button from the action and registers it for you, so toolbar buttons track \fBsetEnabled\fR/\fBsetChecked\fR.
.SS "Bind menu entries"
.PP
A menu row is not a widget, so \fBregister\fR cannot grey it. \fBaddMenuItem\fR creates the command entry and registers that index. \fBsetEnabled\fR then uses \fBentryconfigure \-state\fR. The index is stored as a number at bind time.
.CS
::tkutils::tkuaction::addMenuItem    $menu save
::tkutils::tkuaction::registerMenu   save $menu ?index?   ;# already-created row
::tkutils::tkuaction::unregisterMenu save $menu ?index?
.CE
.SS Groups
.CS
::tkutils::tkuaction::groupDefine imageLoaded {zoom_in zoom_out fit rotate}
::tkutils::tkuaction::groupSet    imageLoaded 0|1 ?$w?  ;# enable/disable the whole set
::tkutils::tkuaction::groupAdd    imageLoaded crop
::tkutils::tkuaction::groupList   ?name?
::tkutils::tkuaction::reset                          ;# drop all actions and groups
.CE
.SS Notes
.IP \(bu
Registered widgets are reconfigured generically (\fB\-state\fR, pressed state, \fB\-image\fR). Menu command entries follow \fBsetEnabled\fR through \fBaddMenuItem\fR / \fBregisterMenu\fR.
.IP \(bu
Without \fB$w\fR, \fBsetEnabled\fR / \fBgetEnabled\fR / \fBgroupSet\fR are process\-global (0.1). With \fB$w\fR, only widgets and menu entries in that toplevel change. A child is resolved with \fBwinfo toplevel\fR. Menu widgets are themselves toplevels, so the first non\-Menu ancestor is used. A later two\-argument \fBsetEnabled\fR clears window overrides. \fBinvoke\fR always uses the global flag.
.IP \(bu
Errors carry \fB{TKUTILS TKUACTION <REASON>}\fR (\fBOPTION\fR, \fBNOACTION\fR, \fBNOGROUP\fR, \fBWINDOW\fR).
.SS Demo
.CS
tclsh examples/demo-tkuaction.tcl
.CE
